W: 2. It was by a woman's treacherous hand
W: That I was condemned to dee
W: Beneath a ledge at a window she stood
W: And a blanket she threw o'er me.
W:
W: Chorus:
W: Sae rantingly, sae wontonly
W: Sae dauntingly gaed he
W: He played a tune an' he danced aroon
W: Beneath the gallows tree.
W:
W: 3. Well the laird o' Grant, that highlan' sa'nt
W: That first laid hands on me
W: He played the cause on Peter Broon
W: To let Macpherson dee.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 4. Untie these bands from off my hands
W: And gie to me my sword
W: There's nae a man in a' Scotland
W: But I'll brave him at a word.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 5. There's some come here to see me hanged
W: And some to buy my fiddle
W: But before that I do part wi' her
W: I'll brak her thro' the middle.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 6. He took the fiddle into both his hands
W: And he broke it o'er a stone
W: Says there's nae other hand shall play on thee
W: When I am dead and gone.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 7. O, little did my mother think
W: When she first cradled me
W: That I would turn a rovin' boy
W: And die on the gallows tree.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 8. The reprive was comin' o'er the brig o' Banff
W: To let Macpherson free
W: But they pit the clock a quarter afore
W: And hanged him to a tree.
W: (Chorus:)
%
